.TH VIDMODE 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
vidmode \- report or select console video mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vidmode
.RI [ mode " [" discipline ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no operands, report the current console's columns, rows and
output discipline. Otherwise request a change and read back the result.
At most two words are accepted.
.TP
.B 40, 80
Select native 40- or 80-column display, with 24 rows.
.TP
.B hq, card
Select the UltraTerm 80-column display.
.TP
.B vt, apple
Select VT-style or Apple output discipline.
.TP
.B onehead
Let monitor selection follow the active console.
.TP
.B dualhead
Hold monitor selection for a second display.
.PP
For example,
.B vidmode 80 vt
requests both geometry and discipline.
Availability depends on the hardware detected by this build.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/VIDMODE  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
chvt(1), stty(1), reset(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 for a refused mode or non-console output, 2 for usage errors.
.SH BUGS
This controls the current console through standard output. Unsupported hardware modes are refused, not emulated.
